From 4df97f91b85373f227ae6f830f899ac6bb8de262 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:43:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pop-up top diverter: plunges come down into the Orion lanes
 and bumpers

Every launch rode the top arch all the way round, down the left orbit and
onto the left flipper. A rubber post (r 4 mm) now pops up against the top of
the arch above the Orion lanes while a ball waits in the shooter lane and for
its launch. The plunged ball clips it about 30 degrees off centre and is
knocked down into the lanes, guide tips and pop bumpers. It drops at the
launched ball's first playfield switch (or 3 s after launch), so orbit shots
from the flippers loop as before; it starts down in the table data.

- Holding the left flipper keeps the post down: the plunge goes round, lands
  in the left cradle, and the left ramp within 6 s is still the SUPER SKILL.
- Plunger spring variance +-3 % (physical, per launch) and a per-game physics
  random stream, so full pulls and touch taps are not identical every time.
- plungerMinLaunch 500 -> 800 mm/s so a 20 % pull clears the shooter lane
  gate (soft pulls no longer fall back a quarter of the time).
- Drawn as a glowing amber post when up, a faint socket when down, with a
  coil thunk and a ring flash as it rises; help text, README and DESIGN.
- Tests: diverter rise/drop and super skill (rules), plunges with the post
  up/down plus the robustness sweep with the post up for half the balls.

plunge-map (40/style): full top 42% lanes 78%, strong 45%/72%, medium
40%/63%, soft 33%/57% (no fall-backs), tap 35%/65%; both flippers about even.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MRNPNtaUcQXCKgby8bGVXz
